  "src/Templates/Boilerplate/Bit.Boilerplate/specs/workarounds.md": [
    "- **Cause:** while it has nothing to say, the read-aloud status of each answer (`.bit-aimac-ras` of `BitAiMessageActions`, Bit.BlazorUI.AI {V}) is hidden with `position: absolute`. `BitAiMessageList`, the transcript's scroll container, is not positioned, so the status is placed against the chat's root instead, where the transcript neither scrolls nor clips it.",
    "- **Upstream:** https://github.com/bitfoundation/bitplatform/issues/14995 (Bit.BlazorUI.AI {V}, reported 2026-11-13).",
    "- **Cause:** `BitAiVoiceInput` (Bit.BlazorUI.AI {V}) marks a recording for the app's own transcriber, with a countdown and a class on its root, but the browser's own speech recognition, which the landing page dictates with, gets only the checked state of its `BitToggleButton`. That it listens, and that the browser refused the microphone, is said only in its visually hidden live region.",
    "- **Upstream:** https://github.com/bitfoundation/bitplatform/issues/14996 (Bit.BlazorUI.AI {V}, reported 2026-11-13)."
  ],
